  "release_notes": "Enhances automated rollback logic for unified rollouts: proactive detection for shadow -> canary regressions, multi-metric thresholds, and safer staged rollouts. Backwards compatible configuration defaults preserved.",
  "description": "Motivation: reduce regression blast radius by detecting model-quality regressions earlier during shadow and canary phases and automatically initiating safe rollbacks. Summary: this PR adds a proactive detector that observes shadow traffic signals, promotes early-stage metric-based rollbacks for canary and shadow flows, and extends the rollout policy config with multi-metric thresholds, grace windows, and noise-tolerant aggregation. Design highlights: 1) proactive-detector service hooks into the existing metrics pipeline and computes rolling z-scores + weighted aggregates across accuracy/error/latency; 2) new policy config 'proactive.shadow_canary' with parameters: lookback_ms, z_threshold, metric_weights, grace_period_ms, min_sample_count; 3) safer rollback action: when triggered we first scale down new variant to 0% traffic for canary then continue shadow-only mode for 1x grace window before full rollback; 4) comprehensive telemetry: rollout-events, detector_alerts, and traces added to the console and can be routed to customer observability. Backwards compatibility: default rollout policy remains unchanged; new proactive behavior is off by default and gated behind the config flag 'enable_proactive_shadow_detector' and Linear task ENG-7123. Checklist: - [x] implement detector and integrate with rollout state machine - [x] add config + validation and defaults - [x] add unit and integration tests for noisy signals - [x] update console UI with detector alerts and timeline annotations - [x] add docs and release notes - [x] run perf benchmarks to confirm negligible latency impact Tests and validation: unit tests for z-score logic and weighted aggregation, rollout integration tests for canary/shadow lifecycles, e2e with synthetic traffic (see canary-e2e job). CI: initial run failed on a flaky rollout test; rerun passed. Rollout plan: feature flagged, staged rollout to internal canaries for 48h, then opt-in for customers, doc updates and migration guide provided. References: ENG-7123, ENG-7340, SUP-9012.",
